# Creamy Tomato Soup

Based on [Chrissy Teigen Cravings](https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/252973/cravings-by-chrissy-teigen-with-adeena-sussman) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251202235345/https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/252973/cravings-by-chrissy-teigen-with-adeena-sussman/)), pg. 45

{ rating="5" image="creamy_tomato_soup.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 6 Tbsp [Olive Oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] 2 medium [onion]{ ing="onion" }, rough dice
- [ ] 8 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, chopped
- [ ] 2 (28 oz) can [whole peeled tomatoes]{ ing="whole-peeled-tomatoes" } in juice
- [ ] 2 cup [low sodium chicken]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken" } or vegetable broth
- [ ] 1 tsp [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [pepper]{ ing="pepper" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }
- [ ] [Side bread]{ ing="side-bread" } or grilled cheese

## Recipe

1. In the dutch oven, heat [oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } and cook the [onion]{ ing="onion" } until translucent (about 10 min). Add the [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } and cook an additional minute
1. Add the [tomatoes]{ ing="whole-peeled-tomatoes" }, broth, [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }, [pepper]{ ing="pepper" }, and optional extra [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
1. Bring to a boil then reduce heat to medium-low and simmer until liquid reduces slightly (~15 min)
1. Removing the pot from heat, use an immersion blender to blend the soup until smooth

   1. (Alternatively, use a regular blender, but you’ll need to let the soup cool for longer and be careful about allowing the steam to escape while blending)
   1. Add the [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" } and blend for a few more seconds
1. Season with additional salt, pepper, and/or sugar to taste
